# Benchmarks & Evaluations
# Tracked in full. This is the paper's evidence base:
#   tasks_*.json              task specifications (18-task suite + subsets)
#   *_results*.json           scored evaluations (macro, ablation, dense, multiskill, routing)
#   checklists_v2/ checklists_ieee/  compiled strategy artifacts
#   ablations/                per-condition prompts backing the byte-identity matrix
#   raw_outputs_*/            archived model generations (auditability, paper §9)
#   calibration_report.md     judge-vs-execution calibration
__pycache__/

# Working analysis notes — local drafts, not artifact outputs.
# These record how a finding was reached. The findings themselves are in the
# paper and the underlying numbers are in the tracked JSON, so these carry no
# evidence a reviewer needs. Nothing in CI reads them: the machine-checkable
# guard for the compiler is scripts/verify_compiled_artifacts.py, which
# compares SHA-256 digests against the tracked manifest.
benchmarks/COMPILER_PROVENANCE.md
benchmarks/MANUSCRIPT_CORRECTIONS.md
benchmarks/POSITION_BIAS_AUDIT.md
benchmarks/ROUTER_LEVEL1_AUDIT.md

